              "x": 340,
              "y": 16,
              "name": "FAB Group",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "oCNIm",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "MzoZn",
                  "name": "navPanelToggle",
                  "layoutPosition": "absolute",
                  "x": 0,
                  "y": 0,
                  "fill": "$g:sem-background-main"
                },
                {
                  "id": "MhHMH",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "MzoZn",
                  "name": "chatPanelToggle",
                  "layoutPosition": "absolute",
                  "x": 0,
                  "y": 50,
                  "fill": "$g:sem-background-main",
                  "descendants": {
                    "KSlnN": {
                      "library": "lucide",
                      "icon": "message-circle"
                    }
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "context",
      "id": "WQehJ",
      "x": -506,
      "y": 3247,
      "name": "Composer — button visibility",
      "width": 340,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "Composer buttons — what shows when\n\nEmpty: voice (default) + send disabled.\nTyping / expanded: voice (default) + send enabled. On expanded, text wraps around the bottom-right cluster — no reserved empty column.\nRecording: voice switches to active (filled); send stays disabled.\nTranscribing: voice disabled at 40% opacity; send disabled.\nWhile the AI is generating: stop replaces send. Voice is unchanged from the current input state.\n\nTokens — send: $g:sem-chatSendBg, .hover, .pressed, .disabled. Stop reuses $g:sem-chatSendBg. Voice: transparent fill, prim-blue-300 border, prim-blue-600 icon; active swaps to the filled $g:sem-chatVoiceActiveBg; disabled keeps the outline at 40% opacity."
    },
    {
      "type": "context",
      "id": "C0Ly6",
      "x": 6472,
      "y": 5165,
      "name": "Mobile FABs + static pages",
      "width": 340,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "Mobile Menu + Chat FABs\n\nBoth FABs sit stacked in the top-right corner. On static pages — Settings, for now — they stay pinned there as the page scrolls; they do not travel with the content.\n\nThe Menu FAB opens the Menu, not the Dashboard.\n\nFill: $g:sem-navToggleBg — the shell surface they float over, always opaque. Border $g:sem-navToggleBorder, icon $g:sem-navToggleIcon."
    },
    {
      "type": "context",
      "id": "g5gTA",
      "x": 3562,
      "y": 5165,
      "name": "Header bar removed",
      "width": 340,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "No header bar on views or static pages\n\nThe view area no longer has a header bar — there is no “Good morning, Sylvia” chrome above the view. The view uses the full area.\n\nOn static pages that have no generated view (Settings, for now), put the page title in the page container itself. Do not leave it in a header-bar slot — that bar is gone on mobile and desktop."
    },
    {
      "type": "context",
      "id": "Zi6tp",
      "x": 3562,
      "y": 6726,
      "name": "Collapsed-panel FABs",
      "width": 340,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "Collapsed-panel FABs (both panels hidden)\n\nWhen nav and chat are both closed, two 34×34 FABs float over the content: nav (panel-left) on the left, chat (message-circle) on the right. The icons show what will open.\n\nDesktop placement — the view area is max 1024px wide, with a gutter on each side that is min 40px and grows with the viewport (no max). The FABs live in that gutter, top-aligned with the content (spacing-md below the mainPanel top).\n• Default: the FAB floats centered in the gutter.\n• As soon as there is room for a spacing-md (24px) gap to the content, the FAB pins there and stops following the center. The gutter keeps growing; the extra is margin.\n\nMobile: see “Mobile FABs + static pages”.\n\nClose / hide controls use arrows (arrow-left-to-line, arrow-right-to-line). Open / show controls use the panel icons.\n\nBoth use the nav-toggle tokens: fill $g:sem-navToggleBg (opaque), border $g:sem-navToggleBorder, icon $g:sem-navToggleIcon. Hover $g:sem-navToggleHoverBg; pressed $g:sem-navTogglePressedBg with $g:sem-navTogglePressedIcon."
    },
    {
      "type": "context",
      "id": "riTFf",
      "x": -506,
      "y": 2563,
      "name": "Chat close FAB",
      "width": 340,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "Chat close FAB (desktop)\n\nReplaces the chat header. Floats at the top-right of the chat panel, 16px inset. Same hide/show behavior as the old header arrow. Messages scroll underneath; the button never covers the input.\n\nFill stays opaque in every state — $g:sem-chatBg on the desktop chat panel, the shell surface on mobile. Never rgba: text must not bleed through.\n\nBorder is conditional. No outline at rest; draw the 1px $g:sem-chatCloseBorder outline only when content scrolls beneath the button, so it stays distinct from messages passing behind it.\n\nIcon $g:sem-chatCloseIcon (arrow-right-to-line). Hover $g:sem-chatCloseHoverBg; pressed $g:sem-chatClosePressedBg with $g:sem-chatClosePressedIcon."
    },
    {
      "type": "context",
      "id": "Nf3Uh",
      "x": -506,
      "y": 175,
      "name": "Color tokens & dark mode",
      "width": 340,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "Color tokens & dark mode\n\nSpecify roles, not hex. Every color binds a Hemlock token (imported under the g: alias), so dark mode is a theme switch on Hemlock’s 🎨 Colors axis rather than a redesign.\n\nPrimitives are fixed paint: $g:prim-blue-600 is always #3A6AF8, $g:prim-taupe-100 is always #F7F5F0. Never bind primitives on components — bind the semantic role.\n\nSemantic tokens carry the light/dark pair — $g:sem-chatBg, $g:sem-chatSendBg, $g:sem-navToggle*. Flip 🎨 Colors to Dark and every bound color remaps; components are never duplicated for dark.\n\nAccent shifts in dark (per Hemlock): primary prim-blue-600 → prim-blue-500, hover prim-blue-700 → prim-blue-400, disabled send prim-blue-200 → prim-blue-800.\n\nThe FAB rule already covers dark: the fill is the surface underneath, always opaque — never rgba.\n\nThis file defines no local tokens: everything comes from hemlock-library.lib.pen."
    },
